@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Tasco Insurance, Quy tắc bảo hiểm sức khoẻ kết hợp (combined health insurance rules), with
-- PHỤ LỤC 5, the guarantee-hospital list, and the excluded-facility list.  [in:tasco-guarantee-hospitals]
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Sources (row VN-19), each a `pdftotext -layout` rendering in ../../source/raw/:
--   tasco-combined-health.txt      the rules, 19 pages (src:N is line N of this file)
--   tasco-guarantee-hospitals.txt  the guarantee-hospital list, 7 pages (src:tasco-guarantee-hospitals:N)
--   tasco-excluded-facilities.txt  the excluded-facility list, 2 pages (src:tasco-excluded-facilities:N)
-- Retrieved 2026-10-06. Nothing in Vietnamese here is typed by hand: src: lines are generated by
-- tools/vnsrc.py quote, and every other Vietnamese run is checked by tools/vnsrc.py check.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. Days are calendar days unless a name says
-- otherwise (NOTES.md, fork register).
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact,
-- or the contract, the certificate, a medical record or an assessment records it. Whether the
-- fact makes a benefit payable is a rule, and lives in the module for the Article that says so.

§ `Nouns`

§§ `The policyholder (Article 2.3)`

-- Bên mua bảo hiểm. An organisation or an individual. The fields that belong to one kind only
-- are read only for that kind; `date of birth` is NOTHING for an organisation.
DECLARE `The policyholder` HAS
    `an organisation`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully established and operating in Vietnam`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `an individual in Vietnam`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of birth`                                                           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `full civil act capacity when the contract is concluded`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the conditions for buying insurance under the rules, conditions and terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an insurable interest under the law`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the contract is concluded`                                          IS A DATE

§§ `The insured person (Articles 1 and 2.2)`

-- Người được bảo hiểm. Article 1.1 admits a Vietnamese person, or a foreigner residing lawfully
-- in Vietnam; anyone else is `neither`.
DECLARE `A nationality and residence` IS ONE OF
    `Vietnamese`
    `a foreigner residing lawfully in Vietnam`
    `neither`

-- The Article 1.2 conditions are facts as at the start date of the contract (fork F3).
-- `permanent disability or injury, in percent`: the rate a medical assessment gives; 0 if none.
DECLARE `The insured person` HAS
    `nationality and residence`                         IS A `A nationality and residence`
    `date of birth`                                     IS A DATE
    `suffering from a neurological disease`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffering from a psychiatric disease`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffering from leprosy`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffering from cancer`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `permanent disability or injury, in percent`        IS A NUMBER
    `in a period of treatment for illness or injury`    IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The contract and the insured's history with Tasco (Articles 2.6-2.9, 5, 7.3, 10)`

-- The scopes of cover, Article 7.2. The words after each letter are the source's own heading.
DECLARE `A scope of cover` IS ONE OF
    `scope A`   -- death from illness, sickness or maternity
    `scope B`   -- death or bodily injury from accident
    `scope C`   -- illness, sickness or maternity requiring hospitalisation or surgery

-- The two programmes of the Article 8 table: "Chương trình phổ thông", "Chương trình đặc biệt".
-- Which one applies is a rule (by the sum insured), not a fact; see tasco-vn19-ch2-cover.l4.
DECLARE `A programme` IS ONE OF
    `the standard programme`
    `the special programme`

-- The waiting periods a group contract of more than 100 persons may fix for itself (Article 10.1
-- rows 2, 3, 5 and 6 add "(or as agreed in the contract)"). NOTHING: the contract says nothing,
-- and the table's figure applies. A number of days.
DECLARE `Waiting periods agreed in the contract` HAS
    `row 2, hospitalisation for a special disease or a pre-existing condition` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `row 3, ordinary illness`                                                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `row 5, pregnancy complications`                                           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `row 6, childbirth`                                                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- Hợp đồng/Giấy chứng nhận bảo hiểm. A sum insured is NOTHING for a scope the contract does not
-- include (Article 7.3). Every figure here is printed on the contract or certificate; none has a
-- default (NOTES.md section 1).
--   `term in months`: the number of months of insurance, which Article 8 III.4 prorates by.
--   `number of persons insured`: the head count the Article 10.1 columns turn on.
--   `supplementary waiting-period clause stated on the contract`: Article 10.2 applies only when
--     Tasco has adopted it and it is "specified on the contract or certificate".
DECLARE `The contract` HAS
    `start date`                                                IS A DATE
    `end date`                                                  IS A DATE
    `term in months`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `sum insured for scope A`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `sum insured for scope B`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `sum insured for scope C`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `premium`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `a group contract`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of persons insured`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `waiting periods agreed`                                    IS A `Waiting periods agreed in the contract`
    `supplementary waiting-period clause stated on the contract` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The contract immediately before this one, for Article 5 (continuity). NOTHING in `The history`
-- when this is the insured's first contract with Tasco.
DECLARE `The previous contract` HAS
    `start date`               IS A DATE
    `end date`                 IS A DATE
    `the same insured person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `sum insured for scope A`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `sum insured for scope B`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `sum insured for scope C`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The insured's history with Tasco, for Articles 1.1, 5, 10 and 11.17.
--   `start of the insured's continuous participation`: the start date of the first contract in the
--     unbroken chain of renewals that ends with this one (the current start date if there is none).
--   `age when continuous participation began`: the Article 2.30 age at that date.
--   `date of the most recent reinstatement`: ngày khôi phục hiệu lực, if the contract was reinstated.
DECLARE `The history` HAS
    `the previous contract`                            IS A MAYBE `The previous contract`
    `start of the insured's continuous participation`  IS A DATE
    `date of the most recent reinstatement`            IS A MAYBE DATE

-- What has happened to the contract up to the event, for Article 4.1. Each date is NOTHING if it
-- has not happened.
--   `amount already paid under scope A/B/C`: paid under this contract before this claim; for scope C,
--     paid in the current policy year (Article 2.8).
DECLARE `The state of the contract` HAS
    `date the premium was not paid in full or on time`  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of an earlier death or total permanent disability of the insured` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date Tasco terminated for ineligibility under Article 4.1(e)` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `amount already paid under scope A`                 IS A NUMBER
    `amount already paid under scope B`                 IS A NUMBER
    `amount already paid under scope C this policy year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `People and places that treat (Articles 2.16, 2.17)`

-- Bác sĩ. The relation to the insured matters because Article 2.16 excludes doctors who are the
-- insured, or a spouse, parent, parent-in-law or child of the insured, the beneficiary, or the
-- employer or an employee of the policyholder.
DECLARE `A relation to the insured` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `the insured`
    `a spouse, parent, parent-in-law or child of the insured`
    `the beneficiary`
    `a spouse, parent, parent-in-law or child of the beneficiary`
    `the employer of the policyholder`
    `an employee of the policyholder`

DECLARE `The treating doctor` HAS
    `holds a lawful practising licence recognised by Vietnamese law`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `treating within the licence and the field of training`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `relation to the insured`                                            IS A `A relation to the insured`
    `registered to practise as required`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- Cơ sở y tế. The kinds Article 2.17 says a medical facility does NOT include, and `a facility of
-- none of those kinds`.
DECLARE `A kind of facility` IS ONE OF
    `a facility of none of the excluded kinds`
    `a place of rest or convalescence, or of rehabilitation`
    `a facility for the elderly only`
    `a facility for withdrawal from alcohol, drugs or other stimulants`
    `a facility for treating mental disorders or leprosy`
    `a workplace medical unit`
    `a private traditional-medicine clinic or diagnosis centre`

DECLARE `The treating facility` HAS
    `name`                                                         IS A STRING
    `a lawful facility for medical examination and treatment in Vietnam` IS A BOOLEAN
    `able and equipped to diagnose, treat and operate`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `equipped for inpatient treatment, daily monitoring and outpatient treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind`                                                         IS A `A kind of facility`

§§ `The insured event (Articles 2.5, 2.10-2.15, 2.18-2.23, 7, 8, 9)`

-- What the event is: tai nạn (accident), ốm đau, bệnh tật (illness, sickness), thai sản (maternity).
DECLARE `A cause` IS ONE OF
    `an accident`
    `an illness`
    `maternity`

-- The rows of the Article 8 table, by their Roman and Arabic numbers.
DECLARE `A benefit` IS ONE OF
    `I.1 death from illness, sickness or maternity`
    `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident`
    `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident`
    `II.3 temporary injury from accident`
    `III.1 hospitalisation in Western medicine`
    `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine`
    `III.3 surgery`

-- Facts about the illness, as the medical records show them (Articles 2.11, 2.12, 2.14).
--   `a special disease`: the illness is one of those Article 2.11 lists, determined from the
--     medical records (src:93). The list itself is carried in tasco-vn19-ch1-general.l4.
--   `treated within the 3 years before the start date`, `symptoms or onset before the start date,
--     known to the insured`: the two limbs of Article 2.12, measured from the start date or the
--     most recent reinstatement date of THIS contract (fork F9).
DECLARE `The illness` HAS
    `a special disease`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `treated within the 3 years before the start date`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `symptoms or onset before the start date, known to the insured` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Maternity events, for the waiting periods of Article 10 and the definition in Article 2.15.
DECLARE `A maternity event` IS ONE OF
    `a pregnancy complication`   -- Article 2.15
    `childbirth`                 -- sinh đẻ, sinh nở
    `other maternity care`       -- maternity that is neither (routine care, a premature birth: fork F14)

-- A hospital stay (Article 2.18). `hours in hospital` is NOTHING where the hospital does not record
-- hours on the medical file, which is the case the source's date formula is for.
--   `actual reasonable cost of treatment`: the cost assessed as actual, necessary and reasonable
--     (Article 2.24), before anything another insurer paid.
DECLARE `A hospital stay` HAS
    `admission date`                                    IS A DATE
    `discharge date`                                    IS A DATE
    `hours in hospital`                                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `admission and discharge procedures completed`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `actual reasonable cost of treatment`               IS A NUMBER
    `days already paid this policy year, same kind of medicine` IS A NUMBER

-- A surgery (Article 2.19). `percentage in the surgery table` is the rate the surgery table gives
-- ("Bảng tỷ lệ trả tiền bảo hiểm phẫu thuật") for this kind of surgery. [cell:tasco-combined-health:459-462]
-- That table is NOT in the deposited source, so
-- it is an input, and NOTHING when the caller does not have it.
DECLARE `A surgery` HAS
    `date of surgery`                                                     IS A DATE
    `by licensed surgeons, by hand or with medical equipment, in a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Ministry of Health list of surgeries`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage in the surgery table`                                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `cost of consultation, anaesthesia, the operation and the operating room` IS A NUMBER

-- The bodily consequence of an accident (Articles 2.20-2.23, 8 II, 9).
DECLARE `A consequence of an accident` IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `total permanent disability by loss`        -- 2.21(a) first sentence, a listed loss
    `total permanent disability by paralysis or assessment` -- 2.21(a), paralysis, blindness, or 81% or more
    `partial permanent disability by loss`      -- 2.22(a) first limb
    `partial permanent disability by loss of function` -- 2.22(a) second limb, and other assessed cases
    `temporary injury`                          -- 2.23

-- `percentage in the injury table`: the rate the Bảng tỷ lệ trả tiền bảo hiểm thương tật gives for
-- this injury, for a person of normal health treated reasonably (Article 9, second paragraph).
-- Not in the deposited source: an input, NOTHING when the caller does not have it. A number of
-- percent (30 for 30%), as are both table percentages.
-- `date the consequence began`: the date of death; for a disability, the day the loss or the
--   loss of function began; for a temporary injury, the day of the injury.
-- `date of certification`: the day the disability was certified (Articles 2.21(b), 2.22(b));
--   for a death or a temporary injury, the same day as `date the consequence began`.
DECLARE `An accidental injury` HAS
    `consequence`                                IS A `A consequence of an accident`
    `date the consequence began`                 IS A DATE
    `date of certification`                      IS A DATE
    `percentage in the injury table`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `actual reasonable cost of treatment`        IS A NUMBER
    `amount already paid for this accident`      IS A NUMBER

-- The circumstances that the exclusions of Article 11 turn on, one per limb, each a fact a witness
-- or a record could establish. The list on a claim names those present; a circumstance not named
-- is absent. Numbers (alcohol readings) are separate fields of `A claim`.
DECLARE `A dangerous activity` IS ONE OF                    -- Article 2.26
    `racing`
    `surveying`
    `exploration`
    `mountain or rock climbing` HAS `using guidance equipment or protective gear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `skiing`
    `parachuting`
    `surfing`
    `deep-sea diving` HAS `with a hard helmet and an oxygen tank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hunting on horseback`
    `wrestling`
    `boxing`
    `martial arts`
    `rugby`

DECLARE `A circumstance of the event` IS ONE OF
    `an intentional act of the insured`                                         -- 11.1
    `an intentional act of a lawful heir of the insured`                        -- 11.1
    `alcohol, beer, drugs or a similar stimulant used by the insured caused it` -- 11.2
    `the insured was driving a vehicle`                                         -- 11.3
    `the insured was driving having used drugs, addictive or similar stimulant substances` -- 11.3
    `the insured broke the law and must serve a criminal sentence`              -- 11.4
    `the insured broke traffic law while driving a vehicle`                     -- 11.4
    `the insured broke a rule of a local authority, an agency or a social organisation` -- 11.4
    `treatment or medication not as the treating doctor directed`               -- 11.5
    `aviation, other than as a ticketed passenger`                              -- 11.6
    `military exercises, military training, or combat in the armed forces`      -- 11.6
    `training for or competing in a professional sport`                         -- 11.6, 2.25
    `taking part in` HAS `the activity` IS A `A dangerous activity`             -- 11.6, 2.26
    `hospitalisation for neurasthenia, physical debility, a mental disorder, a sleep disorder, insomnia, spinal degeneration or spina bifida` -- 11.7
    `treatment or surgery of a congenital disease or defect`                    -- 11.8, 2.13
    `an injury, or an indication for treatment or surgery, existing before the start date` -- 11.8
    `treatment or surgery at the insured's own request`                         -- 11.8
    `bone-marrow failure, leukaemia or artificial kidney dialysis`              -- 11.9
    `malaria, tuberculosis or an occupational disease`                          -- 11.9, 2.14
    `treatment of a sexually transmitted disease`                               -- 11.10
    `illness related to HIV or AIDS`                                            -- 11.10
    `experimental or scientifically unrecognised treatment`                     -- 11.11
    `free treatment services at a hospital`                                     -- 11.11
    `cosmetic treatment, cosmetic surgery, or orthopaedic correction`           -- 11.11
    `supplying, maintaining, fitting, repairing or replacing a medical device or a prosthesis` -- 11.12, 2.28, 2.29
    `family planning, infertility, assisted reproduction, sexual dysfunction, artificial insemination, hormone therapy or gender change` -- 11.13
    `the insured took part in a fight, not confirmed as self-defence`           -- 11.14
    `hospitalisation for a check-up or medical assessment unrelated to treatment` -- 11.15
    `vaccination or preventive medicine, not after an accident or an animal or insect bite` -- 11.15
    `degeneration of hearing or sight, cataract, or a natural refractive error` -- 11.16
    `a catastrophe: earthquake, volcano, tsunami, radiation, asbestos, war, civil war, strike, terrorism or riot` -- 11.18
    `an epidemic declared by a competent authority`                             -- 11.18

-- The claim: one benefit of the Article 8 table, claimed for one insured event.
--   `date of the insured event`: the day the risk arose (the accident; the onset of the illness or
--     of the maternity event), which Article 10 and Article 12.2 count from.
--   `date treatment began`: Article 10 also refuses cover where treatment began in a waiting period.
--   `the illness`, `maternity event`, `the stay`, `the surgery`, `the injury`: NOTHING where the
--     benefit and the cause do not call for them.
--   `the treating doctor`, `the treating facility`: NOTHING where there was no treatment (a death
--     with none, say).
--   `paid by another insurance contract for the same treatment`: Article 3.
--   `breath alcohol while driving`, `blood alcohol while driving`: Article 11.3, in the units the
--     clause prints (fork F27); NOTHING where no reading was taken.
DECLARE `A claim` HAS
    `the policyholder`                         IS A `The policyholder`
    `the insured person`                       IS A `The insured person`
    `the contract`                             IS A `The contract`
    `the history`                              IS A `The history`
    `the state of the contract`                IS A `The state of the contract`
    `benefit claimed`                          IS A `A benefit`
    `cause`                                    IS A `A cause`
    `date of the insured event`                IS A DATE
    `date treatment began`                     IS A DATE
    `in Vietnam`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the illness`                              IS A MAYBE `The illness`
    `maternity event`                          IS A MAYBE `A maternity event`
    `a miscarriage, or a complication that required curettage on a doctor's order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stay`                                 IS A MAYBE `A hospital stay`
    `the surgery`                              IS A MAYBE `A surgery`
    `the injury`                               IS A MAYBE `An accidental injury`
    `the treating doctor`                      IS A MAYBE `The treating doctor`
    `the treating facility`                    IS A MAYBE `The treating facility`
    `circumstances`                            IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of the event`
    `breath alcohol while driving`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `blood alcohol while driving`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `paid by another insurance contract for the same treatment` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The waiting-period table (Article 10.1)`

-- Its columns are headed "Hợp đồng dưới 100 người" and "Hợp đồng nhóm trên 100 người".
DECLARE `A column of the waiting-period table` IS ONE OF
    `contracts of under 100 persons`
    `group contracts of over 100 persons`

-- Its rows, in the source's order.
DECLARE `A row of the waiting-period table` IS ONE OF
    `row 1, accident`
    `row 2, hospitalisation for a special disease or a pre-existing condition`
    `row 3, ordinary illness`
    `row 4, death or total permanent disability from a pre-existing condition, a special disease or maternity`
    `row 5, pregnancy complications`
    `row 6, childbirth`

§§ `What the rules give back`

-- Why a claim is not paid. Each member names the provision that says so.
DECLARE `An exclusion of Article 11` IS ONE OF
    `Article 11.1`, `Article 11.2`, `Article 11.3`, `Article 11.4`, `Article 11.5`, `Article 11.6`
    `Article 11.7`, `Article 11.8`, `Article 11.9`, `Article 11.10`, `Article 11.11`, `Article 11.12`
    `Article 11.13`, `Article 11.14`, `Article 11.15`, `Article 11.16`, `Article 11.17`, `Article 11.18`

DECLARE `A reason for no payment` IS ONE OF
    `the insured is not a person Article 1 admits (Articles 1, 4.1(e))`
    `the contract was not in force on the day of the event (Article 4.1)`
    `the contract does not include the scope this benefit belongs to (Articles 7.2, 7.3)`
    `the event was outside Vietnam (Article 7.1)`
    `the benefit does not answer to the cause of the event (Article 7.2)`
    `the stay is not a hospitalisation as Article 2.18 defines it`
    `the operation is not a surgery as Article 2.19 defines it`
    `the death or disability was not within 180 days of the accident (Article 9)`
    `the disability was certified earlier than Article 2.21(b) or 2.22(b) allows`
    `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`
    `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`
    `excluded by` HAS `the exclusion` IS AN `An exclusion of Article 11`

-- The answer to a claim: the source names both outcomes, and the payable one carries an amount.
DECLARE `The outcome of a claim` IS ONE OF
    `not payable` HAS `reasons` IS A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
    `payable`     HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER

-- Documents for a claim, Article 13, one member per item the Article lists.
DECLARE `A claim document` IS ONE OF
    `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`
    `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`
    `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`
    `13.3(b) injury certificate and the competent authority's injury assessment (original or notarised copy)`
    `13.4(a) financial invoices for medical and related costs (original)`
    `13.4(a) itemised statement of treatment costs`
    `13.4(b) financial invoices or receipts`
    `13.5(a) accident report for an accident in daily life`
    `13.5(b) accident report for an accident at work`
    `13.5(c) driving licence and vehicle registration`
    `13.5(c) police preliminary report and investigation result or conclusion`
    `13.5(c) accident report showing cause, time and place, without a police file`
    `13.6(a) death certificate or extract, and proof of lawful inheritance`
    `13.6(b) conclusion of a doctor or competent authority on the cause of death`
    `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`

-- The parties and acts of the claim procedure (Article 12), for its regulative rules.
DECLARE `A party to a claim` IS ONE OF
    `Tasco`
    `the insured or the beneficiary`

DECLARE `An act in a claim` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice of the insured event`
    `send the claim documents`
    `pay the benefit`
    `give written reasons for refusing the claim`

-- Where an accident happened, for Article 13.5.
DECLARE `A kind of accident` IS ONE OF
    `an accident in daily life`
    `an accident at work`
    `a traffic accident`

§§ `The two lists published with the rules`

-- PHỤ LỤC 5 - DANH SÁCH BẢO LÃNH VIỆN PHÍ, one row per numbered line. [in:tasco-guarantee-hospitals]
-- Columns in the source's
-- order: STT, VÙNG, CƠ SỞ Y TẾ, ĐỊA CHỈ, NỘI TRÚ, NGOẠI TRÚ, RĂNG. [in:tasco-guarantee-hospitals]
-- A mark is TRUE where the source prints "x" in that column (direct billing for inpatient,
-- outpatient or dental care at that facility).
DECLARE `A row of the guarantee list` HAS
    `number`     IS A NUMBER
    `region`     IS A STRING
    `facility`   IS A STRING
    `address`    IS A STRING
    `inpatient`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `outpatient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dental`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- DANH SÁCH CƠ SỞ Y TẾ LOẠI TRỪ, columns STT, TỈNH, HỆ THỐNG CSYT, ĐỊA CHỈ CSYT. [in:tasco-excluded-facilities]
-- A row may name several facilities ("PKĐK Elizabet; PKĐK Khang Thái; ...") [in:tasco-excluded-facilities]
-- and several addresses (CS1, CS2).
DECLARE `A row of the excluded-facility list` HAS
    `number`     IS A NUMBER
    `province`   IS A STRING
    `facilities` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `addresses`  IS A LIST OF STRING
